  "dashboard": {
    "autoRerun": false,
    "cards": [
      {
        "id": "intro",
        "kind": "text",
        "size": "2x2",
        "title": "Same mass, three sections",
        "options": {
          "markdown": true,
          "text": "Three **2 m steel cantilevers of the same mass per metre** (7.77 kg/m): a round bar, a square bar and an **IPE 100** on its strong axis. One tip force pushes all three down. Pick the **load**, press **Run**, and open the **3D View**: the beams are coloured by the bending stress of their outer fibre (grey 0, dark red at the yield stress 235 MPa). The 3D deflection is drawn **x10 (exaggerated)** by default; pick x1 in the view for true scale.\n\nFirst eigenfrequencies: round 6.42 Hz, square 6.57 Hz, IPE 29.4 Hz. A sine at the round bar's frequency (the default 6.42 Hz) shows resonance."
        }
      },
